WEBVTT

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.509
down a specially fabricated carpet

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:03.265
designed to allow him to travel

00:02:03.265 --> 00:02:05.381
as fast as humanly possible.

00:02:05.381 --> 00:02:07.052
Jesse Owens, on the other hand,

00:02:07.052 --> 00:02:10.643
ran on cinders, the ash from burnt wood,

00:02:10.643 --> 00:02:12.880
and that soft surface stole far more energy

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.657
from his legs as he ran.

00:02:14.657 --> 00:02:17.620
Rather than blocks, Jesse
Owens had a gardening trowel

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.447
that he had to use to dig holes
in the cinders to start from.

00:02:21.447 --> 00:02:23.551
Biomechanical analysis of the speed

00:02:23.551 --> 00:02:26.095
of Owens' joints shows that had been running

00:02:26.095 --> 00:02:27.609
on the same surface as Bolt,

00:02:27.609 --> 00:02:30.120
he wouldn't have been 14 feet behind,